 "speech": {
  "language": "en",
  "text": "Hypothyroidism. Is it chronic? I get this question almost every day. Hypothyroidism simply means that your body is not producing enough thyroid hormones, the one that controls your stress, your sleep, your anxiety, gut health, skin, hair and more. In most people, yes, it is chronic. The reason is that the root cause is almost never looked into or addressed. But do you know that chronic doesn't mean permanent? Yes. When you improve your gut health, balance your body nutritionally along with good regular physical activity, management, good sleep and good immunity, your symptoms start to get better healing starts. So instead of asking if it's chronic, ask yourself, what is slowing down my thyroid? What must I start doing to enable healing? Remember, that's where true healing starts, not with pills.",
